{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf5j2mYDHn2bNtnrugWFf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Conventions in this repository:**\n- Errors are thrown as `ApiException` subclasses from controllers\n- `ResourceNotFoundException` (HTTP 404) for missing resources with `ErrorCode.RESOURCE_NOT_FOUND`\n- `ConflictException` (HTTP 409) for state conflicts with appropriate error codes\n- All error codes are centralized in `ApiError.kt:ErrorCode` enum\n- Controllers return `ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus).body(...)` for successful operations\n- `@PostMapping` decorator for state-changing operations\n\n**Affected files (cannot be avoided):**\n1. `ShipmentController.kt:22-56` — Add POST confirm endpoint at line after the `list()` method\n2. `ApiError.kt:31-37` — Add new ErrorCode for shipment state conflict (e.g., `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS`)\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — Add tests for the confirm endpoint behavior\n\n**Risks:**\n- If I choose the wrong error code name, it won't match API conventions (though the enum is closed)\n- Breaking existing tests if I misunderstand the idempotent behavior\n- Not persisting the confirmed shipment if I forget to save\n\n**Open questions:**\n- The ticket doesn't specify the exact error code to use when a shipment is CANCELLED and can't be confirmed. I'll use `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS` as the most semantic choice that follows the existing pattern.\n\nNow I'll move to DESIGN phase.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **`ApiError.kt`:** Add a new error code enum value `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS` to represent when a shipment cannot transition due to its current status (specifically when trying to confirm a CANCELLED shipment).\n\n2. **`ShipmentController.kt`:** Add a new endpoint method annotated with `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")`. The method should:\n   - Take the shipmentId from the path\n   - Check if the shipment exists (throw 404 if not)\n   - If status is CREATED: update it to CONFIRMED, save, and return the updated shipment (200)\n   - If status is CONFIRMED: return the shipment unchanged (200) — idempotent retry succeeds\n   - If status is CANCELLED: throw ConflictException with 409 and `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS` error code\n\n3. **`ShipmentControllerTest.kt`:** Add four test methods:\n   - `confirmCreatedShipmentMovesToConfirmed()` — confirms a CREATED shipment and checks status changed\n   - `confirmConfirmedShipmentIsIdempotent()` — confirms an already CONFIRMED shipment and succeeds\n   - `confirmCancelledShipmentReturns409()` — confirms a CANCELLED shipment and gets 409 conflict\n   - `confirmNonExistentShipmentReturns404()` — confirms a non-existent shipment and gets 404\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\n- Could have created a separate `ShipmentService` class to handle business logic instead of putting it in the controller. Rejected because the codebase has no service layer — the controller directly uses the repository, and adding one would be unrelated refactoring beyond the scope.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\nSuccess case (CREATED → CONFIRMED):\n1. POST request arrives at controller\n2. Repository finds shipment with that ID\n3. Shipment status is CREATED\n4. Update shipment object with status = CONFIRMED\n5. Call repository.save(updated)\n6. Return ResponseEntity.ok(updated)\n\nIdempotent case (already CONFIRMED):\n1. POST request arrives at controller\n2. Repository finds shipment with that ID\n3. Shipment status is already CONFIRMED\n4. Return ResponseEntity.ok(shipment) — no update needed\n5. Caller receives 200 OK with unchanged shipment\n\nConflict case (CANCELLED):\n1. POST request arrives at controller\n2. Repository finds shipment with that ID\n3. Shipment status is CANCELLED\n4. Throw ConflictException(SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS, message)\n5. GlobalExceptionHandler catches it\n6. Returns ResponseEntity with 409 and error envelope\n\nNot found case (no shipment):\n1. POST request arrives at controller\n2. Repository.findById returns null\n3. Throw ResourceNotFoundException(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, message)\n4. GlobalExceptionHandler catches it\n5. Returns ResponseEntity with 404 and error envelope\n\n**Test strategy:**\n- Test 1: Create a shipment in CREATED state, confirm it, verify response status is 200, response body has status CONFIRMED\n- Test 2: Create and confirm a shipment, then call confirm again with same ID, verify 200 response and status still CONFIRMED\n- Test 3: Create a cancelled shipment directly in repository, attempt confirm, verify 409 response with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS error code\n- Test 4: Attempt to confirm a shipment that doesn't exist, verify 404 response with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND error code\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":369,"cache_read_input_tokens":17550,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":369},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b178fd91-7a71-4002-9c90-3d4c5c28c19c","uuid":"7f324d3c-c3ff-4e72-ba33-18e5fab9fa40","timestamp":"2026-09-15T18:49:10.492Z","request_id":"req_011Cf5j2m2wjR7kSe7vDzYX7"}
